From 27342457f5835f348e5e5dfe6dbffb143c90c9d5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 18:47:23 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] lifecycle guard heredoc masking: close the four
 fail-open shapes from review 5879950534

- Wrappers: only stdin-passing wrappers with an explicit per-wrapper option allowlist peel to a
  data consumer (timeout/nice/ionice/nohup/setsid/stdbuf/env/command/exec/eatmydata/sudo/doas).
  Any other option word refuses masking: env -S'bash -s' / --split-string=, exec -a NAME,
  sudo -D/-R/--chdir/-s. The strict walk must land where _peel_transparent_prefixes lands.
- Nested heredocs are judged only for the executed-path walk (strip_inert_heredoc_bodies(...,
  nested=True)); text scanners keep seeing nested bodies, so a rewritten or stdin-hijacked body's
  lifecycle text still blocks. The outer owner must hand its single, non-<<- body unchanged to a
  stdin shell: bash/sh/... (no -c, no script operand), ssh whose remote command is such a shell
  with no operators, or $SSH resolved from an earlier plain assignment. sed ... <<'R' | bash,
  bash <<-'R', an unknown $CMD and shadowed ssh/bash names mask nothing.
- Function-body consumers: never cat (its output is its body); python/osascript bodies stay
  visible to text scans when the command could hand a function's output to a shell
  (|, $(, `, <(, eval, source, .).

Tests: test_lifecycle_guard_heredoc_walk.py 63 -> 96 cases (16 must-refuse shell-runs-body rows,
all pass on origin/main and fail on 004c14deb336; 12 untrusted-owner and 5 trusted-owner strip
unit cases). 670 passed across lifecycle_guard*/terminal*/self_repo_guard.

